INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.OPS OPS-DEGRADED-2: share the qnfo-ops D1 breaker across isolates (OPS-DEGRADED-1 keeps it per isolate)',
 'QNFO.OPS; charter pillar autonomy; roadmap row RM-S1-REDUNDANCY-1 (id 5). CONTEXT: OPS-DEGRADED-1 (PR 7726, qnfo-ops 2.67.0, live 2026-11-05T05:14:59Z) put an in-isolate circuit breaker in qnfo-ops/worker.js between the lines "// ---- OPS-DEGRADED-1:BEGIN" and "// ---- OPS-DEGRADED-1:END": three D1 overload errors in 60 s open it for 60 s, tools that write qnfo-audit (OPS_D1_WRITING_TOOLS) are then refused with HTTP 503 + Retry-After, GET /health carries a degraded block. GAP: the state lives in the module variable __opsD1Breaker, so every isolate needs its own three errors and a cold isolate still sends its first writes to the overloaded database. WHAT TO CHANGE (only inside that block, execTool and the /v1/ideas route): share the open state through the existing KV binding OPS_CACHE_KV: on a trip put key "ops:d1-degraded" with value {until, since} and expirationTtl 60; add an async step that reads the key at most once every 5 s per isolate (cache the answer in the module variable) and sets __opsD1Breaker.until from it, called at the top of execTool and of the /v1/ideas branch before opsD1Gate. A KV error must never refuse or fail a tool: log console.error(JSON.stringify({ worker: "qnfo-ops", where: "ops-degraded-kv", error: ... })) and carry on. WHAT NOT TO TOUCH: OPS_D1_WRITING_TOOLS and opsD1WritesNow (which tools are refused), the 503 body and Retry-After, the order in execTool (unwrap, gate, policy shadow), any D1 read on /health (/health must stay D1-free), tools outside the list. TESTS (offline, no network): extend qnfo-ops/ops-degraded.test.mjs with a fake KV: a trip written by isolate A (a second module instance via a data: import) is seen by isolate B within 5 s; a KV that throws changes nothing; run every qnfo-ops/*.test.mjs (qnfo-ops/patch-budget.test.mjs fails on an untouched main in some Windows checkouts: compare with git show origin/main). RELEASE: python scripts/worker_release.py bump qnfo-ops --minor --note "OPS-DEGRADED-2 ..." then cp qnfo-ops/worker.js qnfo-ops/deployed-current.worker.js (the tool refuses to copy a source with imports; the pair must stay byte-identical), python scripts/pr_fast_guards.py, take the work claim on file:qnfo-ops/worker.js first (it is the most contended file; merge origin/main, never rebase). VERIFY LIVE after the deploy: GET https://qnfo-ops.q08.workers.dev/health shows degraded.shared true and the capability ops-degraded-shared; python scripts/deploy_probes.py --live qnfo-ops prints ok. DEFINITION OF DONE: merged, deployed, the two /health facts read live, marker OPS-DEGRADED-2 in worker.js. PREDICTION: in the next qnfo-audit overload window, after the first trip on any isolate no D1-writing tool call reaches the database on another isolate within 5 s (before: per isolate). FALSIFIER: a Workers log line "ops-degraded-refusal" is missing on a second isolate during an overload window while "ops-degraded-trip" appeared on the first.' || char(10) ||
 'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-ops/worker.js' || char(10) ||
 'code-anchor: function opsD1Gate(now, name, args) {' || char(10) ||
 'code-probe: {"paths":["qnfo-ops/worker.js"],"contains":"OPS-DEGRADED-2"}',
 'session:W2-E-wrap', 'code', 'medium', 'open', unixepoch() * 1000, unixepoch() * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE instr(title, 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.OPS OPS-DEGRADED-2:') = 1 AND status = 'open');

