 'edit-near: new file (copy the header of migrations/2026-11-05-w2e-tp3b-lifecycle-attach.sql: APPLY-BY ci, DB qnfo-audit, one Rollback line, CAUSE-MAPPED; no BACKUP needed for UPDATE only)' || char(10) || char(10) ||
 'QNFO.OPS; charter pillar autonomy; roadmap rows 134, 6, 10, 131. These rows are finished in code and wait for a reading that only time produces; the status moves only with the reading, never before (BRIEF rule: never close to lower a count). Write ONE migration with the flips whose probe passes, leave the others for a later pass and say which in the PR. Each step: probe (read-only, qnfo-audit, indexed), expected reading, then the UPDATE.' || char(10) ||
 'STEP 1, row 134 RM-TP-9-DEPLOY-NO-LOCKOUT (needs now >= 2026-11-05T06:27Z): SELECT count(*) FROM deployment_history WHERE deployed_at > ''2026-10-06T06:27'' AND status != ''success'' AND (notes LIKE ''%10143%'' OR notes LIKE ''%10144%'') must read 0. Then UPDATE roadmap_implementation SET status = ''verified'', verified_at = datetime(''now''), evidence = evidence || '' || <date> verified: 0 of <total> deployment_history rows name 10143/10144 in 30 days'' WHERE id = 134 AND status = ''built''. A non-zero count is a defect: read the rows, open a ROADMAP-1 issue, do not flip.' || char(10) ||
 'STEP 2, row 6 RM-S4-BENCHMARK-1: SELECT last_value, state FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = ''coding_battery_pass_rate'' must read state MEASURED (the run ops_config code_battery_state "cb-1-2026-11-05-0208" ends at i = n = 76); also read benchmark_results rows with run id cb-1 and report_card_inputs where key LIKE ''coding_battery_%''. Then UPDATE row 6 to status ''built'' with the measured pass rate per model in the evidence. If the pass rate is 0.95 or more for two runs the battery is saturated: file cb-2 (harder tasks) as a ROADMAP-1 issue instead of closing.' || char(10) ||
 'STEP 3, rows 10 and 131 (SESSION-AUTOCONTINUE-1): SELECT id, ts, text FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind = ''ops_session_continue'' ORDER BY ts LIMIT 3 must return a row (a durable agent session spent its round budget and continued). Then UPDATE both rows to status ''implemented'' quoting the run id. If seven days pass with kind ''ops_agent_session_budget'' rows but no ops_session_continue row, that is a defect in qnfo-ops (SESSION-AUTOCONTINUE-1 block) to file with a code-task.' || char(10) ||
 'WHAT NOT TO TOUCH: no other row, no metric, no trigger; do not edit a merged migration; do not set a status from a reading older than the step. DEFINITION OF DONE: the migration merged and applied (migration_runs ok), the three rows read the new status, evidence quotes the readings; the closing probe on this issue passes by itself.',
